---
// Egypt — Section 06: "The Weighing of the Heart"
// Theatrical composition with balance metaphor.
---

<section
  class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[var(--egypt-obsidian)] py-section"
  aria-labelledby="weighing-heading"
>
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-landing px-container-x sm:px-8 xl:px-14">
    <!-- Chapter marker -->
    <p
      class="mb-4 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--egypt-gold)]/60"
    >
      06 &mdash; The Weighing of the Heart
    </p>

    <!-- Balance composition -->
    <div class="relative flex flex-col items-center py-16 lg:py-24">
      <!-- THE HEART vs THE FEATHER -->
      <div class="flex w-full max-w-2xl items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div class="text-center">
          <p
            class="font-display text-headline-2 uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--egypt-ochre)]"
          >
            The Heart
          </p>
          <p
            class="mt-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/50"
          >
            Weight of a life
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-center">
          <p
            class="font-display text-headline-2 uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--egypt-gold)]"
          >
            The Feather
          </p>
          <p
            class="mt-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/50"
          >
            Truth of Ma'at
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Balance line -->
      <div class="relative my-12 h-px w-full max-w-2xl" data-balance-line>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[var(--egypt-gold)]/40"></div>
        <!-- Fulcrum -->
        <div
          class="absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 size-3 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 rotate-45 bg-[var(--egypt-gold)]"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Central quote -->
      <p
        class="max-w-lg text-center font-display text-headline-3 uppercase leading-snug tracking-wide text-white"
      >
        A life was judged by the weight of a heart.
      </p>

      <!-- Explanation -->
      <div
        class="mt-12 grid max-w-3xl gap-8 text-center sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4"
      >
        <div>
          <p
            class="font-display text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--egypt-gold)]"
          >
            Ma'at
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/60">
            Goddess of truth, justice, and cosmic order. Her feather was the
            measure of a righteous life.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p
            class="font-display text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--egypt-gold)]"
          >
            Anubis
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/60">
            The jackal-headed god who guided the deceased and operated the
            scales of judgment.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p
            class="font-display text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--egypt-gold)]"
          >
            Osiris
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/60">
            Lord of the underworld, presiding over the final verdict from his
            throne.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p
            class="font-display text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--egypt-gold)]"
          >
            Ammit
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/60">
            The Devourer. Part crocodile, part lion, part hippopotamus. If the
            heart was heavy, she consumed it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
